ored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.prop-cpgs-equiv"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.prop-cpgs-equiv"],"id":"long.prop-cpgs-equiv","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Proposition 12.3 (Infinitely many positive skips are equivalent to half-membership)","locator":"Long record Proposition 12.3, p. 134, label prop:cpgs-equiv","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Define\n$$\n\\mathrm{CPGS}\\ :=\\ \\forall N,\\ \\exists c\\ge N,\\ c\\ \\text{skipped by the rational half-greedy\norbit}\\ \\wedge\\ 0<\\ensuremath{r}(1/2)(c-1)\n$$\nThe positivity conjunct is unconditionally true for every skipped $c$ (an odd-denominator parity fact), hence deletable without changing the Prop’s meaning. What survives, $\\forall N\\,\\exists c\\ge N$ skipped, is exactly $(\\mathtt{greedyMersenneSkippedSupport}(1/2)).\\mathrm{Infinite}$, so\n$$\n\\mathrm{CPGS}\\ \\Longleftrightarrow\\ \\mathrm{HALF}.\n$$*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.prop-cpgs-equiv","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.prop-cpgs-equiv","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.prop-cpgs-equiv%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_cpgs_equiv%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.prop-cpgs-equiv%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_cpgs_equiv%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_cpgs_equiv"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.prop-cpgs-equiv%22%2C%2